# Tracked root reports that the section-2 `*` rule was silently swallowing. Each is in
# the index, so it ships today and `*` does not untrack it, but a deny-by-default
# allowlist that leaves its own tracked files unlisted is a trap: `git check-ignore`
# reports them ignored, and the next `git add` after an unlink recreates a tracked-looking
# file that no clone receives. Audit 2026-10-05, `git check-ignore --no-index -v`.
!/COHORT-UPGRADE.md
!/CONVERGENCE-MAP.md
!/DEAD-CODE-REPORT.md
!/FLOW-READINESS.md
!/LIVE-READINESS-MATRIX.md
!/PITCH.md
!/ROADMAP-LIVE.md
!/RUBRIC-MAP.md
!/WALLET-MATRIX.md
!/WAVE-DELTA.md
!/legal/
!/legal/**
# `!/docs/MIDNIGHT-INTEGRATION.md` alone does not work: git never descends into an
# excluded directory, so the directory itself has to be re-included first (the gotcha in
# this file's own header). `*` still ignores every other file under docs/.
!/docs/
!/docs/MIDNIGHT-INTEGRATION.md

# Evidence scripts are tracked (R3)
!evidence/
!evidence/**

# Campaign harness dirs (R7C)
!/e2e/
!/e2e/**
!/clickmap-harness/
!/clickmap-harness/**
# Push/release tooling. push-kit/ci.yml is the tracked CI definition; .github/ is ignored
# above, so this directory is the only place CI is defined. A directory must be
# re-included before its contents can be.
!/push-kit/
!/push-kit/**
# Audit discovery tables are tracked (R9/M2)
!/audit/
!/audit/**

# release hygiene (generic build artifacts)
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.convex/
*.tgz
*.log
*.webm
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.tools/
midnight-level-db/
hardening/
.hoplite/

